<title>FRANCE: Bull posts 64 mln Ffr H1 97 net profit.</title>
<headline>Bull posts 64 mln Ffr H1 97 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French unless stated)</p>
<p>     Net					gain 64 vs  loss 612</p>
<p>     Operating				gain 75 vs  loss 331</p>
<p>     Turnover				  11,341 vs  10,847</p>
<p>	  NOTE - Bull gave the figures in a statement. It said it</p>
<p>was the first time it had positive positive first-half net earnings since 1988. It confirmed that it expected a &quot;substantial&quot; increase in 1997 net profits compared with the 376 million franc gain in 1996. The group said on February 18 it was aiming for a substantial increase in 1997 profits.</p>
<p>Bull also said that on a constant exchange rate basis sales rose one percent.</p>
</text>
